      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "This article discusses several issues related to therapies that are considered \"complementary\" or \"alternative\" to conventional medicine. A definition of \"complementary and alternative medicine\" (CAM) is considered in the context of the evolving health care field of complementary medicine. A rationale for pain physicians and clinicians to understand these treatments of chronic pain is presented. The challenges of an evidence-based approach to incorporating CAM therapies are explored. Finally, a brief survey of the evidence that supports several widely available and commonly used complementary therapies for chronic pain is provided."
      },
